er locked on himself for over a week  when you induce food insecurity  to a country whose purpose is to  modernize and make people's lives better  i think it adds a certain twist that  that you know  people here and the leadership here are  are not  are not so comfortable with for the past  two years china has touted its approach  towards containing the virus and pointed  towards its rampant spread in the west  as a marker of its superiority this  could break the narrative that uh  china's system is better at doing this  especially if it really explodes in the  next few weeks  so we could be at quite an inflection  point uh in how kobut evolves and and  how the world comes to see china's  performance on kobit but how its own  people see it is what matters the most  and authorities will need to get a  handle on the situation quickly to  prevent people's frustration from  spiraling any further  well earlier i spoke to fabian ketchumer  who filed that report  yeah so basically the city has been  separated into three different  categories um if you live in a  residential compound meaning your  apartment complex your neighborhood  community where there were um cases  detected within the last week that means  you cannot um even leave your flat if  you um live in a compound where there  were no cases detected in the last week  but within the last  two weeks so basically the last uh  14 days and you're allowed to leave your  flat but um can only go within your  gated community you're not allowed to go  to the street and only for those people  who live in a neighborhood community  where there were no cases for the last  two weeks um they are allowed to go to  the street now but only in a confined  area and there's really not much to do  so i mean public transportation is  basically shut all the public facilities  are shut so i mean it is an easing but a  very cautious one and as soon as there's  one only one um single case within your  whole neighborhood the um uh community  shuts down again so it's really  precarious right so you can travel to  shanghai we're hearing from these  restrictions that you've just mentioned  um what's your sense of how serious the  situation is there in shanghai  well it's an emergency situation which  slightly gets better by time but  basically you can see how serious the  situation is by the situation of the uh  by the decision of the u.s consulate in  shanghai today they basically um force  their non-essential staff to fly out um  because they cannot guarantee their  safety and when i talk to residents both  locals and also expats their concerns  are really um quite existential they  fear that the food supply will not be  enough they fear that  they  get separated from their children if the  the children test positive um they also  in general are not so much afraid of the  virus but more afraid of um getting  dragged into the isolation centers  because the hygienic conditions they are  really um  quite devastating and you basically  are locked there with  several thousands of people and it's  really not a pleasant experience so i  think um  it's getting better with time and we saw  the  recent easing but um it's yeah i mean  it's a really tense situation fabian are  there any signs that the government is  perhaps rethinking how it deals with the  virus  so far not really i mean the economic  costs are really going high i mean we  know that  the global supply chains they are really  stressed right now and the service  sector is going down the manufacturing  sector i mean basically 90 percent of  the big cities here in china have been  to some degree affected by lockdowns in  the last um uh two months but um i think  the government is committed also because  of their own propaganda they stated that  um we can manage zero covert uh we are  the only country that can contain the  virus and uh that is a proof of our  superiority and now to change that  course it is really very difficult also  to justify uh towards their own  population  that was fabian kretschmer in beijing
 

